Subject: [mistral.rs] a-request-seeds-its-own-sampling

  An OpenAI `seed` on a request seeds a sampler RNG of the sequence's own, so the same request draws the same tokens and a served reply can be banked byte for byte; unseeded, a sequence draws from the engine's shared RNG as before
  `SamplingParams` carries the field, so every literal of it names it — here, the crates oscar does not build, so the workspace stays whole.

Applies to: 962112d18ea5729fe7acaae5085ce54c2fb66dab
Files: 5

---
